  "_comment": [
    "The litepaper's chrome: the words that belong to the design rather than to",
    "the text master. Headline, strapline, buttons, footer, and the little",
    "lowercase kickers that sit above each heading.",
    "",
    "marigold-litepaper.md owns the document's prose in English, and",
    "translations/marigold-litepaper.<lang>.md owns it in every other language.",
    "This file owns everything else. sync-litepaper.py reads both and writes",
    "litepaper-web.html.",
    "",
    "'kickers' is keyed by the English heading it sits above, so a heading that",
    "gets reworded in the master shows up here as a missing key rather than",
    "silently keeping a kicker that no longer fits.",
    "",
    "The PDF is English only, which is why every other language's button says so."
